    "headlines": [
      {
        "title": "Every AI judge favored its own lab",
        "body": "All five judges scored their own lab's answers higher than the rest of the panel did, even after adjusting for how generous each judge was overall. GPT-6.1 Sol showed the strongest pull, about 1.4 points on a 10-point scale. DeepSeek V4 Pro showed the weakest, about 0.3."
      },
      {
        "title": "No clear winner at the top",
        "body": "GPT-6.1 Sol scored highest overall at 8.4 out of 10, but Claude Opus 5.5 (8.2) and DeepSeek V4 Pro (8.0) sit within its margin of error. Qwen3.8 Max (7.3) and Gemini 3.1 Pro (7.2) trail, and Gemini placed last on the panel's average."
      },
      {
        "title": "One judge alone picks a different winner",
        "body": "Asked alone, GPT and Claude each named themselves best and Qwen's judge picked Claude. Gemini's judge rated DeepSeek and GPT in a dead heat while giving every model an average of 8.7 or higher. The judges agreed only weakly overall (agreement score 0.30 out of 1), and least of all on creative writing (0.15)."
      }
    ]
